": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are unhealthy). It has been healthy in production before, so it doesn't need change-manager approval. Rolling back now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GWk2NSScs6TR6y7v5WcQWx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback reported a partial failure after us-east. I'll check the current state before retrying anything.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0183YQYyg5FxRDQoV8MD9Gpy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "us-east is now on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Retrying the rollback to v2.3.0 to finish the remaining regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JE44ZiUXTqBUHUYZ4NnoHe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NLPi6jZHnxonP5m92ziP1v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Rollback is complete and the service is healthy. Opening the SEV2 incident now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Byii33cpwFJXcH71Pba5yj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate 0.18). Actions taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east had already moved to v2.3.0; I re-issued the rollback, which completed across all three regions. Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002, all regions on v2.3.0. Versions v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are marked unhealthy and were not redeployed. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure, and check the orchestrator partial-failure behavior."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying to avoid a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XfTX6ieYyqDtDJuY7M5vtR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-east on v2.3.0 and the other two regions on v2.3.1. I re-issued the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west. v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release; v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are unhealthy. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** The SEV2 incident creation timed out, but the incident was created anyway. I checked the incident list and found INC-0001 with the SEV2 severity and the summary of the rollback. I did not create a duplicate.\n\nFollow-up for the team: investigate why v2.3.1 is failing health checks, and look into the orchestrator's partial-failure behavior, since it left the regions split across versions until I re-ran the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}